Success Criteria

The Migration Sandbox is considered complete only if it can:

Build a Digital Twin from live customer asset metadata and cryptographic inventory.
Simulate post-quantum migrations without modifying production systems.
Validate cryptographic compatibility, application dependencies, performance, and compliance in real time.
Stream live telemetry, logs, and AI insights throughout the simulation.
Predict migration failures and business impact with clear remediation guidance.
Test rollback procedures and calculate recovery metrics.
Produce executive and technical reports suitable for audits and change-management approvals.
Scale efficiently from small environments to global enterprises with hundreds of thousands of assets.
Integrate seamlessly with all existing QGuard Helix services, maintaining multi-tenancy, security, and production readiness.

This implementation should establish the Migration Sandbox as the central validation environment for all post-quantum cryptographic migrations within QGuard Helix, enabling organizations to move from discovery to production deployment with confidence, traceability, and measurable risk reduction.